 from accident hazards and provides adequate supervision to prevent accidents.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0805":{"code":"F-0805","title":"Ensure each resident receives and the facility provides food prepared in a form designed to meet individual needs.","category":"Nutrition and Dietary Deficiencies","concept":"food_nutrition","concept_label":"Food, nutrition & hydration"},"cms-f0725":{"code":"F-0725","title":"Provide enough nursing staff every day to meet the needs of every resident; and have a licensed nurse in charge on each shift.","category":"Nursing and Physician Services Deficiencies","concept":"staffing","concept_label":"Staffing & supervision"},"cms-f0761":{"code":"F-0761","title":"Ensure drugs and biologicals used in the facility are labeled in accordance with currently accepted professional principles; and all drugs and biologicals must be stored in locked compartments, separately locked, compartments for controlled drugs.","category":"Pharmacy Service Deficiencies","concept":"medication","concept_label":"Medication management"},"cms-f0865":{"code":"F-0865","title":"Have a  plan that describes the process for conducting QAPI and QAA activities.","category":"Administration Deficiencies","concept":"administration","concept_label":"Administration & records"},"cms-f0868":{"code":"F-0868","title":"Have the Quality Assessment and Assurance group have the required members and meet at least quarterly","category":"Administration Deficiencies","concept":"administration","concept_label":"Administration & records"},"cms-f0882":{"code":"F-0882","title":"Designate a qualified infection preventionist to be responsible for the infection prevent and control program in the nursing home.","category":"Infection Control Deficiencies","concept":"infection_prevention","concept_label":"Infection prevention"},"cms-f0550":{"code":"F-0550","title":"Honor the resident's right to a dignified exi